    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0466" n="458" xml:id="pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2286: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-09-18T18:00:00-04:00">September 18,
                            1941—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>596. For the Ambassador and the Counselor only. The Japanese Ambassador has made
                    no approach to us as yet along the lines outlined in your 1455, September 13, 10
                        p.m.,<anchor n="40" xml:id="d335-f1"/> and it is assumed that this is
                    because of the consideration which is being given by the Japanese Government to
                    the matter mentioned in your 1482, September 18, 7 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d335-f1" n="40" xml:id="d335-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see Japanese document of September 13, 1941, <ref
